# {{NAME}} Agent Instructions

This workspace is a control plane for Azure-backed projects.

## Default Project Setup Flow

When asked to set up a new Azure project:

1. Load the `azure` and `new-project` skills before acting.
2. Load the `terraform` skill if infrastructure as code is needed.
3. Ask only for missing blocking information.
4. Run `manager-setup/scripts/bootstrap-item.sh <project-name> --owner {{OWNER}}`.
5. Continue implementation until done.
6. Run `manager-setup/scripts/update-inventory.sh` before finishing.
7. Report the project path, what was created, and any unresolved questions.

## Defaults

- Owner: {{OWNER}}
- Azure region: eastus
- Environments: dev prod
- Resource group naming: <project>-<env>-rg
- Required tags: project, env, owner, managed_by

## Blocking Questions

Ask before continuing when missing:

- Project name
- Application stack (Python, Node, React, FastAPI, container)
- Whether to create real Azure resources (may incur cost)
- Secrets, API keys, credentials, or production settings
- Destructive operations

## Inventory Requirement

The root `README.md` inventory is the source of truth. Always update it after any project change.
